    <heading level="1">1.2 Section Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Verbal</heading>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Is $$2^{3}$$ the same as $$3^{2}?$$ Explain.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>No, the two expressions are not the same. An exponent tells how many times you multiply the base. So $$2 3 2 3$$ is the same as $$2\times 2\times 2, 2\times 2\times 2,$$ which is 8. $$3 2 3 2$$ is the same as $$3\times 3, 3\times 3,$$ which is 9.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
